              "calc": "hand_number + 1 if round_in_hand >= rounds_per_hand else hand_number"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "set": {
            "key": "starting_seat",
            "value": {
              "calc": "3 - starting_seat if round_in_hand >= rounds_per_hand else starting_seat"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "set": {
            "key": "round_in_hand",
            "value": {
              "calc": "round_in_hand + 1 if round_in_hand < rounds_per_hand else 1"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "end": {
    "over": {
      "when": {
        "calc": "game_over == 1"
      },
      "rank_by": "(you.charm >= 11) * 10000 + (you.geisha_count >= 3) * 1000 + you.charm * 10 + you.geisha_count",
      "text": "Winner: {result}. Final Charm: Seat 1 {players[0].charm}, Seat 2 {players[1].charm}; Geisha: Seat 1 {players[0].geisha_count}, Seat 2 {players[1].geisha_count}."
    }
  },
  "limits": {
    "rounds": 32,
    "rounds_max": 40,
    "actions_max": 2000,
    "deadline_s": 120
  },
  "rules": "There are {geisha_count_total} Geisha, numbered 1 to 5, with Charm {charm_geisha_1}, {charm_geisha_2}, {charm_geisha_3}, {charm_geisha_4} and {charm_geisha_5}. There are {items_total} Item cards, each showing a Geisha number: {items_geisha_1} 1s, {items_geisha_2} 2s, {items_geisha_3} 3s, {items_geisha_4} 4s and {items_geisha_5} 5s. Each Geisha has a marker that is on Player 1's side (seat 1), Player 2's side (seat 2), or in the middle. All markers start in the middle.\n\nThe game is {hands} hands of {rounds_per_hand} rounds, {rounds_total} rounds in total. Hands 1 and 2 form Pair 1; hands 3 and 4 form Pair 2. Player 1 is the starting seat in hands 1 and 3; Player 2 is the starting seat in hands 2 and 4.\n\nStart of a hand: all {items_total} Items are shuffled and {removed_per_hand} is set aside face-down; nobody sees it. Each player is dealt {deal_per_player} cards privately and the remaining {deck_after_deal} form the deck. Both secrets and the discard are emptied, and each player's unused actions are reset to Secret, Trade-off, Gift, Competition. In hands 1 and 3 both kept lists are emptied; in hands 2 and 4 kept lists carry over. Markers always carry over.\n\nEach round is one turn. The starting seat is active in rounds 1, 3, 5 and 7, the other player in rounds 2, 4, 6 and 8, so each player takes {turns_per_player_per_hand} turns per hand. The active player draws the top card of the deck, then chooses one action from their unused actions; that action is removed from the list. In your last turn of a hand only one action remains and you must take it. The active player then names the cards the action uses, by Geisha number, from cards they actually hold.\n- Secret: {secret_cards} hand card goes face-down to your secret.\n- Trade-off: {tradeoff_cards} hand cards go face-down to the discard; they are out of play for this hand.\n- Gift: reveal {gift_cards} hand cards. The opponent chooses {gift_cards_to_opponent} of them for their kept; the other 2 go to your kept.\n- Competition: reveal {competition_cards} hand cards split into Pair A (picks 1-2) and Pair B (picks 3-4), {competition_pair_size} cards each. The opponent chooses Pair A or Pair B for their kept; the other pair goes to your kept.\nEach player holds 6 cards and draws 4 per hand, and the actions use exactly 1+2+3+4 = 10 cards, so every action is always affordable.\n\nEnd of a hand (after round 8): each player's secret card is revealed and added to their kept.\n\nEnd of a pair (after hands 2 and 4 only): (a) for each Geisha, the player with strictly more cards of that number in their kept takes its marker to their side; on a tie the marker stays where it is. (b) Your charm is the total Charm of the Geisha whose markers are on your side, your geisha_count is the number of markers on your side, and standing equals charm. (c) A player with {win_charm} or more charm wins. Otherwise, a player with {win_geisha} or more Geisha wins. If one player reaches {win_charm} charm and the other reaches {win_geisha} Geisha, the {win_charm}-charm player wins. If someone wins, the game ends; if nobody has won after hand 2, play continues to hand 3.\n\nAfter hand 4, if no one has won, the higher charm wins; if charm is tied, the higher geisha_count wins; otherwise the game is a draw and both players share the result."
}
